description:
Windows stores a file version as four 16-bit numbers in two 32-bit values (`VS_FIXEDFILEINFO`'s `dwFileVersionMS` and `dwFileVersionLS`). Write the helpers an about box and an update check need:

```cpp
struct Version { std::uint16_t major{ 0 }, minor{ 0 }, patch{ 0 }, build{ 0 }; };

bool parseVersion(const std::string& text, Version& out);
std::string formatVersion(const Version& v, int parts);    // 1 to 4 parts, e.g. formatVersion(v, 3) == "1.2.0"
void packVersion(const Version& v, std::uint32_t& ms, std::uint32_t& ls);
Version unpackVersion(std::uint32_t ms, std::uint32_t ls);
int compareVersions(const Version& a, const Version& b);   // -1, 0 or 1
bool updateAvailable(const std::string& running, const std::string& latest);
```

- `parseVersion` accepts 1 to 4 numbers separated by dots, each 0 to 65535, optionally starting with `v` or `V`; missing parts are 0. Anything else (empty parts, letters, a fifth part, spaces) fails.
- `packVersion`: `ms = major << 16 | minor`, `ls = patch << 16 | build`.
- `updateAvailable` is true only if both strings parse and `latest` is newer.

